1
00:00:01,007 --> 00:00:03,507
♪

2
00:00:03,507 --> 00:00:04,507
Eugeo: ALICE?

3
00:00:04,507 --> 00:00:05,637
( Kirito gasps )

4
00:00:07,807 --> 00:00:10,307
Eugeo: ALICE,
IT’S YOU, ISN’T IT?

5
00:00:21,407 --> 00:00:23,527
( groans )

6
00:00:23,527 --> 00:00:25,327
Kirito: EUGEO!

7
00:00:25,327 --> 00:00:27,907
Alice:
CHOOSE YOUR ACTIONS CAREFULLY.

8
00:00:27,907 --> 00:00:32,667
I HAVE THE RIGHT TO REMOVE UP TO
70% OF YOUR LIFE IF I WISH IT,

9
00:00:32,667 --> 00:00:35,297
AND IF YOU TOUCH ME AGAIN
WITHOUT MY PERMISSION,

10
00:00:35,297 --> 00:00:36,957
I WILL HAVE YOUR HAND.

11
00:00:41,427 --> 00:00:42,717
Eugeo: ALICE.

12
00:00:42,717 --> 00:00:44,467
Kirito: ARE YOU SURE?

13
00:00:44,467 --> 00:00:46,307
’CAUSE IT’S BEEN A WHILE
SINCE YOU SAW HER.

14
00:00:46,307 --> 00:00:47,427
Eugeo: MM-HMM.

15
00:00:47,427 --> 00:00:49,427
Kirito: THEN WE DO
WHAT SHE SAYS...

16
00:00:49,427 --> 00:00:50,767
FOR NOW.

17
00:00:50,767 --> 00:00:52,397
WE CAN ARGUE
OUR CASE WITH HER

18
00:00:52,397 --> 00:00:54,647
AFTER WE GET
INSIDE THE CENTRAL CATHEDRAL.

19
00:00:54,647 --> 00:00:57,317
Alice: ENOUGH DELAYS.

20
00:00:57,317 --> 00:01:00,777
NOW, ELITE DISCIPLE EUGEO,
ELITE DISCIPLE KIRITO,

21
00:01:00,777 --> 00:01:04,197
YOU ARE IN VIOLATION
OF THE TABOO INDEX.

22
00:01:04,197 --> 00:01:07,537
I WILL TAKE YOU INTO CUSTODY,
THEN QUESTION YOU,

23
00:01:07,537 --> 00:01:09,747
THEN EXECUTE YOU.

24
00:01:09,747 --> 00:01:11,287
♪

25
00:01:11,287 --> 00:01:13,577
♪ SHINY SWORD, MY DIAMOND ♪

26
00:01:13,577 --> 00:01:15,457
( singing in Japanese )

27
00:01:26,597 --> 00:01:27,597
♪ IT’S TIME ♪

28
00:01:27,597 --> 00:01:29,427
( singing in Japanese )

29
00:01:45,697 --> 00:01:47,617
♪

30
00:02:57,507 --> 00:02:58,837
( Kirito grunts )

31
00:02:58,837 --> 00:03:01,047
( girls panting )

32
00:03:02,387 --> 00:03:03,387
( Eugeo gasps )

33
00:03:03,387 --> 00:03:04,517
TIESE!

34
00:03:04,517 --> 00:03:05,427
Kirito: RONIE!

35
00:03:14,437 --> 00:03:17,317
Tiese: L-LADY KNIGHT,
FORGIVE OUR INTRUSION

36
00:03:17,317 --> 00:03:19,567
Ronie: WE’D LIKE TO RETURN THESE
TO OUR MENTORS

37
00:03:19,567 --> 00:03:21,407
WITH YOUR PERMISSION.

38
00:03:21,407 --> 00:03:23,327
Alice: VERY WELL. HOWEVER,

39
00:03:23,327 --> 00:03:25,827
I CANNOT ALLOW THESE CRIMINALS
TO CARRY WEAPONS.

40
00:03:25,827 --> 00:03:28,747
I WILL LOOK AFTER THEM.

41
00:03:28,747 --> 00:03:29,707
( Ronie stammers )

42
00:03:32,877 --> 00:03:33,837
Alice: YOU HAVE ONE MINUTE.

43
00:03:33,837 --> 00:03:36,377
SPEAK WITH THEM, IF YOU WISH.

44
00:03:36,377 --> 00:03:37,717
( girls gasp )

45
00:03:41,547 --> 00:03:43,257
Tiese: I’M SORRY, EUGEO.

46
00:03:43,257 --> 00:03:45,597
YOU SHOULDN’T EVEN BE
IN THIS MESS.

47
00:03:45,597 --> 00:03:47,727
I SHOULD. THIS IS MY FAULT.

48
00:03:47,727 --> 00:03:51,097
I WAS DUMB.
I ACTED SO RECKLESSLY.

49
00:03:52,937 --> 00:03:54,977
Eugeo: STOP IT.
YOU’RE NOT TO BLAME.

50
00:03:54,977 --> 00:03:57,897
YOU DID THE RIGHT THING.
YOUR FRIEND WAS IN TROUBLE,

51
00:03:57,897 --> 00:03:59,857
AND YOU DID
WHAT YOU COULD TO HELP.

52
00:03:59,857 --> 00:04:02,447
WHAT HAPPENED IS MY FAULT,
NOT YOURS.

53
00:04:02,447 --> 00:04:03,867
( Tiese whimpers )

54
00:04:03,867 --> 00:04:06,867
Eugeo: YOU HAVE NOTHING
TO BE SORRY ABOUT EVER.

55
00:04:06,867 --> 00:04:08,997
Tiese: I PROMISE,
WHATEVER IT TAKES,

56
00:04:08,997 --> 00:04:10,537
I’LL BECOME
AN INTEGRITY KNIGHT,

57
00:04:10,537 --> 00:04:13,707
AND THEN I’LL BE THE ONE
TO COME AND SAVE YOU,

58
00:04:13,707 --> 00:04:16,247
AND I WON’T STOP UNTIL I DO.

59
00:04:16,247 --> 00:04:18,457
’TIL THEN, DON’T GIVE UP HOPE!

60
00:04:18,457 --> 00:04:21,007
I SWEAR I’LL SAVE YOU!

61
00:04:25,097 --> 00:04:28,597
Ronie: UM,
I BROUGHT YOU SOME LUNCH.

62
00:04:28,597 --> 00:04:30,387
Kirito: UH...

63
00:04:30,387 --> 00:04:31,727
( chains rattle )

64
00:04:31,727 --> 00:04:34,057
Ronie: MAKE SURE TO EAT IT
BEFORE IT SPOILS.

65
00:04:35,687 --> 00:04:37,567
- Kirito: THANKS, RON--
- ( Ronie gasps )

66
00:04:37,567 --> 00:04:40,527
Alice: IT IS TIME. STEP AWAY.

67
00:04:40,527 --> 00:04:42,197
♪

68
00:04:46,527 --> 00:04:47,287
Tiese: NO.

69
00:04:51,617 --> 00:04:53,287
( wings flapping )

70
00:05:23,317 --> 00:05:25,237
♪

71
00:05:41,547 --> 00:05:43,837
Asuna: I WISH THEY’D LET ME
DIVE IN THERE WITH YOU.

72
00:05:43,837 --> 00:05:45,257
MAYBE I COULD GET YOU OUT.

73
00:05:52,727 --> 00:05:54,637
♪

74
00:05:59,517 --> 00:06:01,227
- ( grinding )
- ( footsteps clanking )

75
00:06:04,697 --> 00:06:06,407
OH, EXCUSE ME.

76
00:06:08,487 --> 00:06:09,777
( gasps )

77
00:06:13,867 --> 00:06:17,247
A-A ROBOT!

78
00:06:19,457 --> 00:06:20,667
( gasps )

79
00:06:32,677 --> 00:06:34,427
( whimpers )

80
00:06:34,427 --> 00:06:35,687
Higa: HEY!

81
00:06:35,687 --> 00:06:37,807
YOU’RE SCARIN’ HER, ICHIEMON!

82
00:06:40,517 --> 00:06:42,937
Asuna: WH-WHAT DID YOU
CALL THIS THING JUST NOW?

83
00:06:42,937 --> 00:06:44,897
Higa: HIS NAME. WHAT ELSE?

84
00:06:44,897 --> 00:06:46,697
HE’S ICHIEMON,

85
00:06:46,697 --> 00:06:50,657
AN ELECTROACTIVE MUSCLED
OPERATIVE MACHINE, OR "EMOM."

86
00:06:50,657 --> 00:06:52,947
HE’S ALSO THE FIRST
OF HIS TYPE,

87
00:06:52,947 --> 00:06:55,827
SO, LIKE, WE ADDED
THE "ICHI" AT THE TOP.

88
00:06:55,827 --> 00:06:56,997
"ICHIEMON." GET IT?!

89
00:06:58,827 --> 00:07:01,837
Asuna: A-AND WHAT IS
THIS ICHIEMON DOING ONBOARD?

90
00:07:01,837 --> 00:07:03,247
Higa: WELL, HE’S SOR--

91
00:07:03,247 --> 00:07:04,877
Rinko: I’M USING IT
TO FINE-TUNE A PROGRAM,

92
00:07:04,877 --> 00:07:07,717
AND HIGA HERE
IS GIVING ME HAND WITH IT.

93
00:07:07,717 --> 00:07:10,007
WE’RE LAB PARTNERS AGAIN,
JUST LIKE IN COLLEGE.

94
00:07:10,007 --> 00:07:11,677
( Asuna chuckles ) GOOD MORNING.

95
00:07:13,217 --> 00:07:15,517
Rinko: MORNING. YOU SLEEP WELL?

96
00:07:15,517 --> 00:07:18,767
♪

97
00:07:18,767 --> 00:07:21,727
YOUR PROBLEM IS ITS BALANCER’S
PROCESSOR RUNS SLOW.

98
00:07:21,727 --> 00:07:23,727
CAN’T YOU BUY A FASTER CHIP?

99
00:07:23,727 --> 00:07:25,567
IT’S NOT LIKE
YOU DON’T HAVE THE BUDGET TO.

100
00:07:25,567 --> 00:07:26,937
Higa: YEAH,
BUT COOLING AND BATTERY DRAIN

101
00:07:26,937 --> 00:07:28,647
WOULD STILL BE A PROBLEM.

102
00:07:28,647 --> 00:07:30,987
CONSIDERING THAT, THIS IS
THE BEST THAT WE CAN DO.

103
00:07:30,987 --> 00:07:32,697
ONE OTHER OPTION WOULD BE

104
00:07:32,697 --> 00:07:35,287
TO TUNE THE E.A.P. ACTUATOR
TO PICK UP THE SLACK.

105
00:07:35,287 --> 00:07:36,697
Rinko: SURE,
BUT THE POLYMER MUSCLES

106
00:07:36,697 --> 00:07:39,037
ARE LAST GEN, SO THERE’S THAT.

107
00:07:39,037 --> 00:07:41,077
UPGRADE TO C.N.T.s.

108
00:07:41,077 --> 00:07:43,127
THEY’LL TAKE THE STRAIN BETTER
AND MAKE IT LIGHTER.

109
00:07:43,127 --> 00:07:45,047
Asuna: HMM?

110
00:07:45,047 --> 00:07:46,507
Rinko: UH...

111
00:07:46,507 --> 00:07:47,917
WE’RE IN OUR OWN WORLD
OVER HERE.

112
00:07:47,917 --> 00:07:49,927
SORRY ABOUT THE NOISE.

113
00:07:49,927 --> 00:07:51,047
Asuna: THAT’S OKAY.

114
00:07:52,137 --> 00:07:53,887
IF KIRITO WERE HERE,

115
00:07:53,887 --> 00:07:56,217
HE’D GET A BIG KICK
OUT OF THIS ROBOT OF YOURS.

116
00:07:56,217 --> 00:07:57,677
Higa: ACTUALLY, WE BUILT HIM

117
00:07:57,677 --> 00:07:59,557
’CAUSE THE COMANDANTE
WANTED US TO.

118
00:07:59,557 --> 00:08:02,687
Asuna: WAIT. KIKUOKA DID?
WH-WHAT FOR?

119
00:08:02,687 --> 00:08:04,267
Rinko: IT’S A NEAT IDEA,
ACTUALLY,

120
00:08:04,267 --> 00:08:07,187
BUT I’M NOT SURE
HOW SERIOUS HE IS ABOUT IT YET.

121
00:08:07,187 --> 00:08:09,527
ULTIMATELY, HIS GOAL
IS TO BRING FLUCTLIGHTS

122
00:08:09,527 --> 00:08:11,487
FROM THE UNDERWORLD
INTO OUR WORLD,

123
00:08:11,487 --> 00:08:13,157
BUT THE CATCH IS
THEY’RE GOING TO NEED

124
00:08:13,157 --> 00:08:14,657
SOMETHING
THEY CAN MOVE AROUND IN.

125
00:08:14,657 --> 00:08:16,237
Asuna: SO WAIT.

126
00:08:16,237 --> 00:08:19,287
THE PLAN IS
TO PUT THE A.I.s IN THAT?

127
00:08:19,287 --> 00:08:23,037
Higa: NOT THIS GUY. HE’S JUST
A PROTOTYPE FOR DATA COLLECTION.

128
00:08:23,037 --> 00:08:24,997
WE HAVE A SECOND ROBOT
WITH ONBOARD A.I.

129
00:08:24,997 --> 00:08:26,417
THAT’S WAY MORE ADVANCED.

130
00:08:26,417 --> 00:08:28,127
HE OPERATES
A HECK OF A LOT SMOOTHER.

131
00:08:28,127 --> 00:08:30,797
Asuna: OH, YOU DON’T SAY?

132
00:08:30,797 --> 00:08:33,837
I WONDER WHAT YOU DECIDED
TO CALL THAT ONE.

133
00:08:35,097 --> 00:08:36,807
Higa: NIEMON, OF COURSE!

134
00:08:36,807 --> 00:08:38,847
Asuna: "NI" WHAT? OH.

135
00:08:38,847 --> 00:08:40,137
RIGHT, "NI" MEANS TWO.

136
00:08:40,137 --> 00:08:42,727
ANYWAY, WHY DOES
HAVING ONBOARD A.I.

137
00:08:42,727 --> 00:08:44,647
IN THIS OTHER ROBOT
MAKE IT BETTER?

138
00:08:48,817 --> 00:08:50,187
Rinko: FOR US TO BALANCE,

139
00:08:50,187 --> 00:08:52,817
OUR BRAINS MAKE
LOTS OF MICROADJUSTMENTS.

140
00:08:52,817 --> 00:08:55,237
TO REPLICATE THAT MECHANICALLY
WOULD TAKE A LOT OF TECH

141
00:08:55,237 --> 00:08:58,657
AND A BIGGER BODY
TO HOUSE IT ALL IN.

142
00:08:58,657 --> 00:09:00,447
Asuna: OH.

143
00:09:00,447 --> 00:09:03,787
SO IF A FLUCTLIGHT IS PILOTING
INSTEAD OF A CPU,

144
00:09:03,787 --> 00:09:06,747
THE ROBOT CAN MOVE MORE LIKE
A HUMAN AND ALSO BE SMALLER.

145
00:09:06,747 --> 00:09:09,837
Higa: BINGO! AND THE SMALLER
THE TECH INSIDE,

146
00:09:09,837 --> 00:09:12,547
THE CLOSER IT CAN LOOK
LIKE A HUMAN BODY,

147
00:09:12,547 --> 00:09:14,637
OR SO WE HOPE.

148
00:09:14,637 --> 00:09:17,507
FOR NOW, HE’S STILL
A WORK IN PROGRESS.

149
00:09:17,507 --> 00:09:19,347
NIEMON’S COMING ALONG, THOUGH.

150
00:09:19,347 --> 00:09:21,097
HE’S LOOKIN’ PRETTY HUMAN.

151
00:09:21,097 --> 00:09:22,847
WELL,
HIS SILHOUETTE DOES, ANYWAY.

152
00:09:22,847 --> 00:09:24,307
Rinko: AND MAYBE
ONE OF THESE DAYS,

153
00:09:24,307 --> 00:09:26,307
I’LL GET TO SEE
THE DAMN THING. WAIT!

154
00:09:26,307 --> 00:09:28,227
YOU HAVEN’T
GOTTEN IT TO WALK AROUND

155
00:09:28,227 --> 00:09:30,067
ON ITS OWN YET, HAVE YOU?

156
00:09:30,067 --> 00:09:32,147
Higa: WHAT?
NO, OF COURSE I HAVEN’T.

157
00:09:32,147 --> 00:09:34,907
HIS CPU IS ALL LOADED UP
AND READY TO GO,

158
00:09:34,907 --> 00:09:36,907
BUT NO ONE’S HOME
TO WORK THE CONTROLS,

159
00:09:36,907 --> 00:09:38,197
IF YOU GET MY DRIFT.

160
00:09:38,197 --> 00:09:39,697
Rinko: OH.

161
00:09:39,697 --> 00:09:41,117
- HEY, ASUNA...
- Asuna: HUH?

162
00:09:41,117 --> 00:09:42,247
Rinko: HAVE YOU
HAD BREAKFAST YET?

163
00:09:42,247 --> 00:09:44,077
Asuna: NO, I HAVEN’T.

164
00:09:44,077 --> 00:09:46,877
Rinko: THEN LET’S GO DOWN
TO THE CAFETERIA TOGETHER.

165
00:09:46,877 --> 00:09:50,377
I’D INVITE HIGA, BUT HE ALREADY
MADE PLANS WITH ICHIEMON.

166
00:09:52,207 --> 00:09:54,627
Higa: BON APPÉTIT, LADIES!

167
00:09:54,627 --> 00:09:56,467
( door whooshes )

168
00:10:00,097 --> 00:10:01,137
( Asuna grunts )

169
00:10:01,137 --> 00:10:03,057
♪

170
00:10:05,307 --> 00:10:06,847
( chuckles ) BACK IN A BIT.

171
00:10:13,027 --> 00:10:14,027
HUH?

172
00:10:14,027 --> 00:10:16,657
♪

173
00:10:22,077 --> 00:10:23,197
( Asuna gasps )

174
00:10:26,957 --> 00:10:28,917
Rinko: SOMETHING WRONG, ASUNA?

175
00:10:28,917 --> 00:10:30,627
Asuna: OH. NO, IT’S NOTHING.

176
00:10:30,627 --> 00:10:31,667
Rinko: COME ON.

177
00:10:36,717 --> 00:10:38,637
♪

178
00:10:44,597 --> 00:10:46,227
( footsteps thumping )

179
00:10:53,027 --> 00:10:55,277
Kirito: WE’VE ONLY BEEN HERE
FOR A DAY AND A HALF,

180
00:10:55,277 --> 00:10:57,737
BUT IT FEELS WAY LONGER.

181
00:10:57,737 --> 00:11:00,737
HEY, HOW YOU DOIN’ OVER THERE?

182
00:11:00,737 --> 00:11:02,407
Eugeo: I DON’T KNOW.

183
00:11:02,407 --> 00:11:04,657
THIS WHOLE THING
FEELS LIKE A NIGHTMARE.

184
00:11:04,657 --> 00:11:06,907
I KEEP SEEING
HUMBERT’S ARM FLYING OFF

185
00:11:06,907 --> 00:11:09,417
AND RAIOS SCREAMING AS HE DIED.

186
00:11:09,417 --> 00:11:11,957
Kirito: GET THAT STUFF
OUT OF YOUR HEAD.

187
00:11:11,957 --> 00:11:13,627
START THINKING ABOUT
WHAT WE’RE GONNA DO NEXT.

188
00:11:15,667 --> 00:11:17,547
Eugeo: I DON’T KNOW
WHAT THAT COULD BE.

189
00:11:20,177 --> 00:11:22,597
YOU KNOW,
YOU’RE ABSOLUTELY RIGHT.

190
00:11:22,597 --> 00:11:25,347
WE HAVE TO FIND A WAY
TO BREAK OUT OF THIS CELL

191
00:11:25,347 --> 00:11:27,137
AND THEN FIGURE OUT
WHAT HAPPENED TO ALICE.

192
00:11:27,137 --> 00:11:29,057
Kirito: YEAH.

193
00:11:29,057 --> 00:11:31,477
IF THERE’S A WAY OUT
OF THIS PLACE, WE’LL FIND IT.

194
00:11:32,857 --> 00:11:34,227
Eugeo: I WONDER...

195
00:11:34,227 --> 00:11:37,067
DID THEY BRING ALICE HERE
EIGHT YEARS AGO?

196
00:11:37,067 --> 00:11:38,317
Kirito: I DON’T KNOW. MAYBE.

197
00:11:38,317 --> 00:11:40,237
( sighs )

198
00:11:40,237 --> 00:11:42,067
SINCE YOU BROUGHT HER UP,

199
00:11:42,067 --> 00:11:44,537
I JUST WANNA BE SURE
OF SOMETHING.

200
00:11:44,537 --> 00:11:48,327
THE KNIGHT THAT CALLS HERSELF
ALICE SYNTHESIS THIRTY,

201
00:11:48,327 --> 00:11:49,867
YOU’RE POSITIVE THAT SHE’S

202
00:11:49,867 --> 00:11:52,207
THE SAME ALICE
YOU’RE LOOKING FOR?

203
00:11:52,207 --> 00:11:53,667
Eugeo: YEAH, I AM.

204
00:11:53,667 --> 00:11:56,957
THOSE BLUE EYES,
GOLDEN HAIR, AND THAT VOICE,

205
00:11:56,957 --> 00:11:58,507
I’D NEVER FORGET THEM.

206
00:11:58,507 --> 00:12:01,177
BUT SHE SEEMED LIKE
A TOTALLY DIFFERENT PERSON.

207
00:12:01,177 --> 00:12:02,797
Kirito: FOR SOMEONE
WHO’S SUPPOSED TO BE

208
00:12:02,797 --> 00:12:05,557
YOUR CHILDHOOD FRIEND,
SHE WHACKED YOU PRETTY GOOD.

209
00:12:05,557 --> 00:12:08,057
BUT IF YOU WANT MY OPINION,
IT COULD BE

210
00:12:08,057 --> 00:12:10,637
SHE’S UNDER SOME KIND
OF MIND CONTROL OR SOMETHING.

211
00:12:10,637 --> 00:12:12,347
Eugeo: BUT I DON’T REMEMBER
SEEING SPELLS LIKE THAT

212
00:12:12,347 --> 00:12:13,897
IN ANY OF OUR TEXTBOOKS.

213
00:12:13,897 --> 00:12:15,897
Kirito: RIGHT,
BUT THE HIGH-RANKING PRIESTS

214
00:12:15,897 --> 00:12:18,357
IN THE CHURCH
CAN MANIPULATE LIFE.

215
00:12:18,357 --> 00:12:21,987
IF THEY CAN DO THAT, THEY CAN
CONTROL SOMEONE’S MIND, TOO.

216
00:12:21,987 --> 00:12:25,327
ALTHOUGH, IF THAT KNIGHT
REALLY IS YOUR ALICE,

217
00:12:25,327 --> 00:12:27,327
WHOSE VOICE DID I HEAR...

218
00:12:27,327 --> 00:12:30,867
TWO YEARS AGO IN THE CAVE?

219
00:12:30,867 --> 00:12:35,037
Girl: KIRITO, EUGEO,
COME AND FIND ME.

220
00:12:35,037 --> 00:12:36,087
I AM WAITING...

221
00:12:38,457 --> 00:12:41,007
AT THE TOP
OF THE CENTRAL CATHEDRAL.

222
00:12:44,597 --> 00:12:47,507
I WILL WAIT THERE FOR YOU BOTH.

223
00:12:47,507 --> 00:12:50,227
Eugeo: RIGHT. YOU TOLD ME THAT.

224
00:12:50,227 --> 00:12:52,057
WHEN YOU AND SELKA
WERE HEALING ME,

225
00:12:52,057 --> 00:12:53,597
YOU SAID YOU HEARD A VOICE

226
00:12:53,597 --> 00:12:55,437
AND THEN SAW SOMETHING
THAT LOOKED LIKE ALICE.

227
00:12:55,437 --> 00:12:57,607
Kirito: YEAH.
SHE SAID SHE’D WAIT FOR US

228
00:12:57,607 --> 00:12:59,277
AT THE TOP
OF THE CENTRAL CATHEDRAL.

229
00:12:59,277 --> 00:13:02,147
AND NOW WE’RE STUCK.

230
00:13:05,157 --> 00:13:06,367
( gasps )

231
00:13:08,987 --> 00:13:10,697
HEY, DO YOU THINK
WE CAN ACCESS

232
00:13:10,697 --> 00:13:12,247
THE STACIA WINDOWS
ON THESE CHAINS?

233
00:13:12,247 --> 00:13:14,457
Eugeo: I NEVER EVEN
THOUGHT TO TRY THAT.

234
00:13:14,457 --> 00:13:16,037
GIVE IT A SHOT.

235
00:13:16,037 --> 00:13:16,707
Kirito: ’KAY.

236
00:13:21,127 --> 00:13:22,587
WHOA. IT WORKED.

237
00:13:26,297 --> 00:13:29,387
Eugeo: AH, WE COULD PULL
ON THESE CHAINS FOREVER,

238
00:13:29,387 --> 00:13:31,097
AND THEY’D NEVER BUDGE.

239
00:13:31,097 --> 00:13:33,347
IF WE’RE GOING
TO BREAK FREE OF THEM,

240
00:13:33,347 --> 00:13:35,937
WE NEED TO GET OUR HANDS
ON A TOOL OR WEAPON

241
00:13:35,937 --> 00:13:37,397
THAT’S AT LEAST CLASS 38.

242
00:13:38,477 --> 00:13:39,857
( Kirito grunts )

243
00:13:39,857 --> 00:13:41,777
YEAH, THAT WON’T DO ANYTHING.

244
00:13:45,107 --> 00:13:46,817
( sighs )

245
00:13:46,817 --> 00:13:48,407
Eugeo: I KNOW
WHAT YOU’RE THINKING,

246
00:13:48,407 --> 00:13:50,197
BUT THE ONLY THINGS
WE HAVE IN HERE

247
00:13:50,197 --> 00:13:53,037
ARE A COUPLE OF BEDS,
WATER SKINS, AND THESE CHAINS.

248
00:13:53,037 --> 00:13:55,997
Kirito: A PAIR OF CHAINS.

249
00:13:55,997 --> 00:13:56,997
( grunts )

250
00:13:56,997 --> 00:13:58,747
Eugeo: UH...

251
00:14:00,457 --> 00:14:03,337
Kirito: YEAH, YOU’RE RIGHT.
WE GOT THESE CHAINS,

252
00:14:03,337 --> 00:14:05,087
TWO OF THESE SUCKERS,

253
00:14:05,087 --> 00:14:06,177
JUST WHAT WE NEED.

254
00:14:06,177 --> 00:14:08,257
Eugeo: WHAT?

255
00:14:08,257 --> 00:14:09,847
( chains clinking )

256
00:14:18,187 --> 00:14:20,017
HANG ON. I HAVE A QUESTION.

257
00:14:20,017 --> 00:14:23,027
IS YOUR IDEA TO USE THE CHAINS
AGAINST ONE ANOTHER?

258
00:14:23,027 --> 00:14:24,777
Kirito: IT TOTALLY IS.

259
00:14:24,777 --> 00:14:27,407
THESE CHAINS OF OURS HAVE
THE SAME DURABILITY LEVEL.

260
00:14:27,407 --> 00:14:29,277
WE’D NEED SOMETHING

261
00:14:29,277 --> 00:14:32,327
WITH AN OBJECT CONTROL AUTHORITY
OVER 40 TO BREAK ’EM,

262
00:14:32,327 --> 00:14:34,197
BUT IF WE SNAP ’EM
AGAINST EACH OTHER,

263
00:14:34,197 --> 00:14:36,247
THAT SHOULD WEAR ’EM DOWN.

264
00:14:36,247 --> 00:14:37,537
JUST FOLLOW MY LEAD, OKAY?

265
00:14:37,537 --> 00:14:38,827
Eugeo: UH...

266
00:14:43,207 --> 00:14:44,297
Kirito: READY, AND...

267
00:14:47,427 --> 00:14:48,427
HELL, YEAH!

268
00:14:48,427 --> 00:14:50,097
Eugeo: NOT SO LOUD!

269
00:14:50,097 --> 00:14:52,097
- YOU’LL WAKE THE GUARD UP!
- Kirito: UH...

270
00:14:53,847 --> 00:14:55,227
( guard snoring )

271
00:14:55,227 --> 00:14:56,437
( mutters )

272
00:14:58,227 --> 00:14:59,687
( both sigh )

273
00:14:59,687 --> 00:15:01,357
Kirito: LET’S GIVE IT
ANOTHER TRY.

274
00:15:03,227 --> 00:15:05,897
Both: READY, AND...

275
00:15:07,447 --> 00:15:08,987
( Kirito groans )

276
00:15:08,987 --> 00:15:10,117
( Eugeo groans )

277
00:15:12,197 --> 00:15:16,457
I THINK THAT KNOCKED
AT LEAST 100 POINTS OFF MY LIFE.

278
00:15:16,457 --> 00:15:18,167
Kirito:
THAT’S A SMALL PRICE TO PAY

279
00:15:18,167 --> 00:15:19,537
FOR FREEDOM, WOULDN’T YOU SAY?

280
00:15:19,537 --> 00:15:20,917
THINGS ARE LOOKIN’ UP.

281
00:15:20,917 --> 00:15:21,917
Eugeo: MM-HMM.

282
00:15:25,127 --> 00:15:26,467
Kirito: ALL RIGHT, THEN.

283
00:15:29,677 --> 00:15:33,057
IF WE DO THIS,
THERE’S NO GOING BACK FOR US.

284
00:15:33,057 --> 00:15:35,637
REMEMBER,
BY BREAKING OUT OF THIS CELL

285
00:15:35,637 --> 00:15:38,227
AND LOOKING
FOR THE TRUTH ABOUT ALICE,

286
00:15:38,227 --> 00:15:42,057
WE’RE DEFYING THE AXIOM CHURCH
AND ITS LAWS.

287
00:15:42,057 --> 00:15:44,897
THAT MEANS FROM NOW ON,
THERE’S NO TIME

288
00:15:44,897 --> 00:15:47,607
FOR SECOND-GUESSING
OR HESITATION.

289
00:15:47,607 --> 00:15:51,197
YOU BETTER MAKE SURE
YOU’RE PREPARED FOR THAT NOW.

290
00:15:51,197 --> 00:15:52,487
OTHERWISE,
YOU SHOULD STAY HERE.

291
00:15:54,487 --> 00:15:56,327
Eugeo: YEAH, I KNOW.

292
00:15:56,327 --> 00:15:59,037
BUT MY MIND’S MADE UP.

293
00:15:59,037 --> 00:16:01,207
IF I CAN RETURN HOME WITH ALICE,

294
00:16:01,207 --> 00:16:04,207
DEFYING THE CHURCH
ISN’T EVEN A QUESTION.

295
00:16:04,207 --> 00:16:07,297
I’LL EVEN DRAW MY SWORD
AGAINST THEM IF I HAVE TO.

296
00:16:07,297 --> 00:16:11,717
I WANT TO MAKE SURE THAT KNIGHT
IS ALICE, AND, IF SHE IS,

297
00:16:11,717 --> 00:16:14,757
I’LL FIND A WAY TO CHANGE HER
BACK TO THE WAY SHE WAS.

298
00:16:14,757 --> 00:16:16,927
THAT’S THE ONLY THING
THAT MATTERS TO ME,

299
00:16:16,927 --> 00:16:19,017
AND NOTHING WILL STOP ME.

300
00:16:19,017 --> 00:16:20,187
REMEMBER WHAT YOU SAID

301
00:16:20,187 --> 00:16:23,017
ON THAT PICNIC
WITH RONIE AND TIESE?

302
00:16:23,017 --> 00:16:24,687
"THERE ARE THINGS YOU SHOULD DO,

303
00:16:24,687 --> 00:16:26,477
EVEN IF THE LAWS
SAY YOU SHOULDN’T."

304
00:16:26,477 --> 00:16:29,697
I UNDERSTAND
WHAT YOU MEANT BY THAT NOW.

305
00:16:31,237 --> 00:16:32,067
Kirito: ALL RIGHT.

306
00:16:37,657 --> 00:16:41,247
YOU SOUND LIKE YOU’RE READY,
SO LET’S GO GIVE ’EM SOME HELL.

307
00:16:50,007 --> 00:16:50,917
( yells )

308
00:16:55,177 --> 00:16:57,217
SWEET. LET’S GO
BEFORE THE GUARD WAKES UP.

309
00:16:57,217 --> 00:16:58,217
Eugeo: RIGHT.

310
00:16:58,217 --> 00:16:59,847
♪

311
00:17:04,437 --> 00:17:05,767
( guard grumbling )

312
00:17:08,397 --> 00:17:10,987
( snoring )

313
00:17:14,277 --> 00:17:16,237
♪

314
00:17:45,557 --> 00:17:47,807
( Kirito sighs ) DOESN’T LOOK
LIKE ANYONE’S FOLLOWING US.

315
00:17:47,807 --> 00:17:49,477
Eugeo: NO WAY. LOOK AT THAT!

316
00:17:49,477 --> 00:17:50,647
Kirito: WHAT’S UP?
IS SOMEONE COMING?

317
00:17:52,277 --> 00:17:53,947
Eugeo: SEE THESE FLOWERS?

318
00:17:54,947 --> 00:17:56,237
I’VE HEARD OF THEM.

319
00:17:56,237 --> 00:17:59,697
KIRITO, THESE ARE ROSES.

320
00:17:59,697 --> 00:18:02,157
Kirito: OH, YEAH. HUH.

321
00:18:02,157 --> 00:18:04,747
NO WAY! THEY ARE ROSES,

322
00:18:04,747 --> 00:18:06,877
AND THIS PLACE
IS CHOCK-FULL OF ’EM!

323
00:18:06,877 --> 00:18:08,997
Eugeo: IT’S RARE TO FIND ONE,
BUT A WHOLE GARDEN FULL...

324
00:18:11,297 --> 00:18:13,337
I CAN’T BELIEVE
WE’RE STANDING HERE.

325
00:18:13,337 --> 00:18:17,007
YOU AND I ACTUALLY MADE IT
TO THE CENTRAL CATHEDRAL.

326
00:18:17,007 --> 00:18:20,387
Kirito: YEAH. WE’RE CRIMINALS,
NOT INTEGRITY KNIGHTS,

327
00:18:20,387 --> 00:18:22,137
BUT WE’RE HERE,
AND THAT’S ALL THAT MATTERS.

328
00:18:22,137 --> 00:18:23,767
Eugeo: IT’S PROBABLY
FOR THE BEST

329
00:18:23,767 --> 00:18:25,437
THAT THINGS WORKED OUT THIS WAY.

330
00:18:25,437 --> 00:18:27,267
IF WE HAD BECOME
INTEGRITY KNIGHTS,

331
00:18:27,267 --> 00:18:29,107
WE MIGHT HAVE
ENDED UP LIKE ALICE.

332
00:18:29,107 --> 00:18:31,187
Kirito: THEY COULD HAVE
GOTTEN IN OUR HEADS

333
00:18:31,187 --> 00:18:33,027
AND SCREWED
WITH OUR MEMORIES, TOO.

334
00:18:33,027 --> 00:18:36,357
I WONDER, IF THEY DO THAT
TO ALL THE INTEGRITY KNIGHTS,

335
00:18:36,357 --> 00:18:40,577
DO THEY FORGET EVERYTHING
ABOUT WHO THEY WERE BEFORE?

336
00:18:40,577 --> 00:18:42,327
Eugeo: WHO KNOWS?

337
00:18:42,327 --> 00:18:45,037
Kirito: YEAH, WELL,
EVEN IF A KNIGHT’S MEMORIES

338
00:18:45,037 --> 00:18:47,457
GOT BLOCKED SOMEHOW,
THEY’D AT LEAST REMEMBER

339
00:18:47,457 --> 00:18:50,837
THEIR PARENTS OR
THE PLACE WHERE THEY WERE BORN.

340
00:18:50,837 --> 00:18:53,547
STUFF LIKE THAT’S
BAKED INTO A PERSON’S SOUL.

341
00:18:53,547 --> 00:18:55,337
IT’D BE IMPOSSIBLE TO SWAP OUT

342
00:18:55,337 --> 00:18:57,547
THOSE KIND OF DETAILS
WITH FAKE ONES.

343
00:18:57,547 --> 00:18:59,047
Eugeo: YOU HAVE A POINT.

344
00:18:59,047 --> 00:19:02,427
THOSE FAKE MEMORIES
WOULD LIKELY BE TENUOUS AT BEST.

345
00:19:02,427 --> 00:19:04,887
WHAT IF THEY WERE
FLYING AROUND WHILE ON DUTY

346
00:19:04,887 --> 00:19:07,227
AND CAME UPON
THE PLACE THEY GREW UP?

347
00:19:07,227 --> 00:19:09,517
ONCE THEY SAW IT,
THEY WOULD KNOW,

348
00:19:09,517 --> 00:19:11,317
AND ALL THEIR MEMORIES
WOULD COME--( gasps )

349
00:19:13,187 --> 00:19:14,687
Kirito: WHAT?

350
00:19:14,687 --> 00:19:17,147
( sighs ) NOT AGAIN.

351
00:19:17,147 --> 00:19:19,157
- ( Eugeo gasps )
- ( Kirito chuckles )

352
00:19:19,157 --> 00:19:20,987
I GET IT!

353
00:19:20,987 --> 00:19:22,527
YOU’RE WORRIED I’LL FIND A WAY

354
00:19:22,527 --> 00:19:24,617
TO GET MY MEMORIES BACK
IN THAT TOWER, AREN’T YOU?

355
00:19:24,617 --> 00:19:25,747
Eugeo: NO!

356
00:19:25,747 --> 00:19:28,577
WELL, A LITTLE. ( sighs )

357
00:19:28,577 --> 00:19:30,287
( Kirito chuckles )

358
00:19:30,287 --> 00:19:31,787
WOULD YOU RELAX?!

359
00:19:31,787 --> 00:19:34,837
Eugeo: DON’T!
STOP IT! LET ME GO!

360
00:19:34,837 --> 00:19:37,797
Kirito: MAN, I TOLD YOU BEFORE
NOT TO WORRY, AND I MEANT IT.

361
00:19:37,797 --> 00:19:41,547
WHETHER I GET MY MEMORIES BACK
OR NOT, WE MAKE A GREAT TEAM,

362
00:19:41,547 --> 00:19:43,257
SO WE’RE STICKIN’ TOGETHER
’TIL THE END.

363
00:19:43,257 --> 00:19:44,847
( Eugeo sighs )

364
00:19:44,847 --> 00:19:46,767
STOP TREATING ME LIKE A KID.

365
00:19:46,767 --> 00:19:49,727
IT’S NOT THAT I DON’T TRUST YOU
TO KEEP YOUR WORD.

366
00:19:49,727 --> 00:19:53,017
YOU’VE ONLY MENTIONED IT
A MILLION TIMES SO FAR.

367
00:19:53,017 --> 00:19:55,857
BUT WHEN I THINK
ABOUT HOW OUR JOURNEY

368
00:19:55,857 --> 00:20:01,067
MIGHT BE COMING TO AN END,
I FEEL--I DON’T KNOW.

369
00:20:01,067 --> 00:20:05,117
Kirito: THE FACT IS
IT’S GONNA END ONE DAY,

370
00:20:05,117 --> 00:20:07,117
BUT DON’T FORGET
WHAT THAT’S GONNA MEAN.

371
00:20:07,117 --> 00:20:10,077
YOU’LL GET ALICE’S MEMORY BACK,

372
00:20:10,077 --> 00:20:11,747
AND THEN YOU’RE
GONNA TAKE HER HOME.

373
00:20:13,917 --> 00:20:16,127
THERE’S ANOTHER GOOD THING
THAT’LL COME OUT OF IT.

374
00:20:16,127 --> 00:20:17,627
YOU’LL GET TO PICK
ANOTHER CALLING.

375
00:20:17,627 --> 00:20:20,427
IT MIGHT LAST
THE REST OF YOUR LIFE,

376
00:20:20,427 --> 00:20:23,547
SO YOU BETTER START THINKING
ABOUT WHAT YOU WANT.

377
00:20:23,547 --> 00:20:26,387
Eugeo: I THINK I STILL HAVE
A BIT OF TIME TO DECIDE.

378
00:20:26,387 --> 00:20:27,807
I KNOW WHATEVER I PICK

379
00:20:27,807 --> 00:20:29,847
WON’T HAVE ANYTHING TO DO
WITH WOODCUTTING.

380
00:20:29,847 --> 00:20:31,727
( Kirito laughs )
NO SURPRISE THERE.

381
00:20:31,727 --> 00:20:32,937
COME ON. LET’S GET GOING.

382
00:20:45,827 --> 00:20:47,617
- Man: AS EXPECTED.
- ( both gasp )

383
00:20:47,617 --> 00:20:50,657
Man: I HAVE TO ADMIRE
MY LADY ALICE’S WISDOM.

384
00:20:50,657 --> 00:20:53,877
EVERYONE THOUGHT ESCAPE
FROM THAT PRISON WAS IMPOSSIBLE,

385
00:20:53,877 --> 00:20:55,627
AND YET MY MENTOR PREDICTED IT.

386
00:20:55,627 --> 00:20:57,707
Kirito: MENTOR?

387
00:20:57,707 --> 00:21:00,417
Man: SHE ORDERED ME
TO CAMP OUT HERE FOR THE NIGHT

388
00:21:00,417 --> 00:21:03,177
IN ANTICIPATION
OF YOUR BREAKOUT.

389
00:21:03,177 --> 00:21:05,847
TO BE HONEST,
I WAS SKEPTICAL YOU’D SHOW UP,

390
00:21:05,847 --> 00:21:07,757
AND, OH, HOW WRONG I WAS.

391
00:21:10,307 --> 00:21:10,977
( Eugeo gasps )

392
00:21:13,767 --> 00:21:16,227
AN INTEGRITY KNIGHT!

393
00:21:16,227 --> 00:21:18,647
Kirito: HIS MENTOR IS ALICE?

394
00:21:18,647 --> 00:21:20,647
Knight: THAT SAID,
YOU’LL BE RETURNING

395
00:21:20,647 --> 00:21:22,777
TO YOUR GLOOMY PRISON SHORTLY

396
00:21:22,777 --> 00:21:25,737
AFTER I ADMINISTER PUNISHMENT
FOR YOUR TRANSGRESSIONS.

397
00:21:28,367 --> 00:21:30,827
YOU’VE BEEN WARNED,
SO PREPARE YOURSELVES.

398
00:21:30,827 --> 00:21:33,077
Kirito: WELL,
HERE’S A WARNING FOR YOU, THEN.

399
00:21:33,077 --> 00:21:35,667
IF YOU THINK WE’RE GONNA
GO BACK THERE WITHOUT A FIGHT,

400
00:21:35,667 --> 00:21:37,247
- YOU’RE CRAZY.
- ( Knight gasps )

401
00:21:37,247 --> 00:21:39,457
♪

402
00:21:39,457 --> 00:21:41,917
( laughs )

403
00:21:41,917 --> 00:21:44,087
SUCH NERVE!

404
00:21:44,087 --> 00:21:46,757
IN HONOR OF YOUR BRAVADO,
I SHALL INTRODUCE MYSELF.

405
00:21:50,887 --> 00:21:54,807
I AM THE INTEGRITY KNIGHT
ELDRIE SYNTHESIS THIRTY-ONE.

406
00:21:54,807 --> 00:21:57,767
I DO NOT HAVE A TERRITORY
TO MY NAME YET,

407
00:21:57,767 --> 00:22:00,357
AS I WAS FRESHLY SUMMONED
ONLY A MONTH AGO.

408
00:22:02,277 --> 00:22:04,697
I DO HOPE THAT FACT
DOESN’T BOTHER YOU.

409
00:22:04,697 --> 00:22:05,947
♪

410
00:22:05,947 --> 00:22:07,617
( singing in Japanese )

